    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "My LDT Final Project aims to utilize the recursive benefits gained from social-psychological interventions - often called WISE Interventions. These interventions have the capacity to improve academic performance for students who are historically and systematically disenfranchised in schools. WISE Interventions can also mitigate negative academic trends that befall students who are habitually disenfranchised by the dominant culture.  These interventions show success in laboratory and school settings. The project will build on these successes but will deliver the interventions to secondary students via an app. Initially, the app will reach to students in traditional middle and high school settings be it a charter, an independent, or a district school. In subsequent phases of the project, the app’s use will extend to students re-entering into those schools from an alternative education setting or a juvenile justice center.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
